Boot. Monte Carlo Algorithm


Draw a bootstrap sample, \({\bf x}_1^{*}\) from \(F_n\) and compute \(\hat{\theta}({\bf x}_1^{*})\).
Repeat (1) \(B\) times yielding \(\hat{\theta}({\bf x}_2^{*})\), \(\dots\), \(\hat{\theta}({\bf x}_B^{*})\) estimates.
Compute: \[\begin{equation*}
\hat{\sigma}_B (\hat\theta)= \sqrt{
\frac{
     \sum_{b=1}^B\left( \hat{\theta}(%
     {\bf x^{*}_i})-\overline{\hat{\theta}^*}\right) ^2
     }{
     (B-1)
     }
}, \quad \overline{\hat{\theta}^*}\equiv \frac 1B\sum_{b=1}^B\hat{\theta}\left( {\bf x}%
_b^{*}\right)
\end{equation*}\]

